cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it as below."
title: "Securities Class Action Social-Media Sentiment Dataset"
abstract: >-
  66,890 X/Twitter message IDs discussing U.S. securities class actions
  (2002-2025), with sentiment and relevance labels from an LLM classifier,
  per-message scores from four off-the-shelf sentiment models (VADER,
  Loughran-McDonald, FinBERT, Twitter-RoBERTa), and a 400-message
  human-annotated gold standard with its codebook and agreement statistics.
  The 845 underlying lawsuits ship as a structured case record - court,
  parties, class period, motion and settlement outcomes, lifecycle dates -
  so message sentiment can be joined to case outcomes directly. Distributed
  as message IDs plus labels; message text is re-hydrated by the user via
  the included tool, in line with X's Developer Agreement.
type: dataset
